dispatch: '--not-a-declared-flag' is not a flag dispatch declares. Declared: --base, --cap, --dry-run, --from, --help, --home, --instants-dir, --lineage-base, --lineage-mode, --milestone, --optype, --override, --porcelain, --profile, --slot, --title. Refused, not ignored: a parser that accepts what no spec declares is a second, hand-maintained copy of the flag list.
fleet dispatch --profile <value> --title <value>
    evaluate every gate, then dispatch one worker
    --profile <value>            (required) the profile directory; its kind is DECLARED in profile.json
    --title <value>              (required) the worker's title; becomes the instantName
    --base <value>               the dispatching base instant
    --optype <value>             append | compact; must agree with the profile's kind
    --from <value>               the DISPATCHING instant. Recorded in the child's .fleet/origin.json so the child's `propose` reaches THIS roadmap instead of its own; required with --milestone
    --milestone <value>          the milestone on --from's roadmap this dispatch is for. Refused unless it is READY and unclaimed; claimed on success, so two instants cannot take one milestone
    --lineage-base <value>       the GIT base to build on, as `repo=sha,repo=sha`. The single authority: rendered into the seed and charter, and `propose --status done`/`complete` refuse if the slot is not there
    --lineage-mode <value>       code (must be AT or DESCENDED FROM the base) | analysis (base fetched but not checked out is fine, and keeps the prebuilt native artifacts valid). Defaults to code
    --slot <value>               a specific enrolled slot instead of the first free one
    --cap <value>                the WIP cap, said out loud
    --override <value>           override the refusing rules WITH A STATED REASON
    --home <value>               the record/pool store root; overrides $FLEET_HOME
    --instants-dir <value>       where instants live; overrides $FLEET_INSTANTS
    --porcelain                  machine form on stdout: tab-separated, no banner (NFR2-7)
    --help                       print this verb's derived usage and exit 0
    --dry-run                    evaluate every gate and CREATE NOTHING; the delta is asserted to be zero

exit codes:
    0  ok
    1  needs attention / check failed
    2  bad input
    3  no capacity
    4  refused by an admission rule
    pane-guard only (FD-10):
    0  safe
    10 queued-text
    11 mid-turn
    12 not-claude
    13 unknown-pane

